Hirata</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ogawa</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kometani</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuwano</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Naito</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuwano</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ono</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>ZD1839 (Iressa) induces antiangiogenic effects through inhibition of epidermal growth factor receptor tyrosine kinase</article-title><source>Cancer Res</source><year>2002</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>2554</fpage><lpage>2560</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Res||62|2554||bib12|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11980649</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hirota</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Murata</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Itoh</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Yodoi</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Fukuda</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Redox-sensitive transactivation of epidermal growth factor receptor by tumor necrosis factor confers the NF-<italic>&#x003ba;</italic>B activation</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>2001</year><volume>276</volume><fpage>25953</fpage><lpage>25958</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Biol Chem||276|25953||bib13|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11337489</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ito</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Takeda</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Sasaki</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Sakon</surname><given-names>M</gi